      * *note Strategy: reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, Choose a strategy for the saturation step
      * *note Variable: symmetricKernel_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value "w", Choose name for variables in the created
        ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the ring $R[It] \otimes{} R/I$ of
        the normal cone of $I$

Description
===========

The normal cone of an ideal $I\subset{} R$ is the ring $R/I \oplus{} I/I^2
\oplus \ldots$, also called the associated graded ring of $R$ with respect to
$I$.  If $S$ is the Rees algebra of $I$, then this ring is isomorphic to
$S/IS$, which is how it is computed here.

