distinguished -- Compute the distinguished subvarieties of a pullback, intersection or cone
*******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = distinguished(f,I)
        L = distinguished(I,J)
        L = distinguished(I)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note BasisElementLimit:
        minimalReduction_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmBasisElementLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value infinity, Bound the number of Groebner basis elements to
        compute in the saturation step
      * *note DegreeLimit: reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value {}, Bound the degrees considered in the
        saturation step. Defaults to infinity
      * *note MinimalGenerators:
        reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMinimalGenerators=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value true, Whether the saturation step returns minimal
        generators
      * *note PairLimit: reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPairLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value infinity, Bound the number of s-pairs considered in
        the saturation step
      * *note Strategy: reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, Choose a strategy for the saturation step
      * *note Variable: symmetricKernel_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value "w", Choose name for variables in the created
        ring
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Suppose that f:S\to R is a map of rings, and I is an ideal of S. Let K be the
kernel of the map of associated graded rings gr_I(S) \to gr_(fI)R.

The distinguished primes p_i in S/I are the intersections of the minimal primes
P_i over K with S/I \subset{} gr_IS, that is, the minimal primes of the support
in R/I of the normal cone of f(I). The multiplicity associated with p_i is by
definition the multiplicity of P_i in the primary decomposition of K.

Distinguished subvarieties and their multiplicity (defined by the distinguished
primes, usually in the global case of a quasi-projective variety and its sheaf
of rings) play a central role in the Fulton-MacPherson construction of refined
intersection products. See William Fulton, Intersection Theory, Section 6.1 for
the geometric context and the general case, and the explanation in the article
Rees Algebras in JSAG (submitted).

This application is illustrated in the code for *note intersectInP:
intersectInP,.

We allow the special cases

distinguished(I,J) := distinguished(f,I), with f:S\to S/J the projection

and

distinguished(I) := distinguished(f,I), with f:S\to S the identity.

which computes the distinguished primes in the support of the normal cone gr_IS
itself. An interesting application is given in the paper

``A geometric effective Nullstellensatz,'' Invent. Math. 137 (1999), no. 2,
427–448 by Ein and Lazarsfeld.

Here is an example showing that associated primes need not be distinguished
primes:

+----------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b]        |
|                            |
|o1 = R                      |
|                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing         |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^2, a*b)    |
|                            |
|             2              |
|o2 = ideal (a , a*b)        |
|                            |
|o2 : Ideal of R             |
+----------------------------+
|i3 : ass I                  |
|                            |
|o3 = {ideal a, ideal (b, a)}|
|                            |
|o3 : List                   |
+----------------------------+

There is one minimal associated prime (a thick line in $P^3$) and one embedded
prime.

+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : distinguished I                  |
|                                      |
|o4 = {{2, ideal (b, a)}, {1, ideal a}}|
|                                      |
|o4 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : intersectInP(I,I)                |
|                                      |
|o5 = {{1, ideal a}}                   |
|                                      |
|o5 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+

