The answer, ideal 1 shows that the second blowup desingularizes the tacnode.

It is not necessary to repeatedly blow up closed points: there is always a
single ideal that can be blown up to desingularize (Hartshorne, Algebraic
Geometry,Thm II.7.17). In this case, blowing-up (x,y^2) desingularizes the
tacnode x^2-y^4 in a single step.

