specialFiberIdeal -- Special fiber of a blowup
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        specialFiberIdeal M
        specialFiberIdeal(M,f)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, or an *note ideal:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a non-zerodivisor
        such that $M[f^{-1}]$ is a free module when $M$ is a module, an element
        in $M$ when $M$ is an ideal
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note BasisElementLimit:
        minimalReduction_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmBasisElementLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value infinity, Bound the number of Groebner basis elements to
        compute in the saturation step
      * *note DegreeLimit: reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value {}, Bound the degrees considered in the
        saturation step. Defaults to infinity
      * Jacobian => ..., default value false
      * *note MinimalGenerators:
        reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMinimalGenerators=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value true, Whether the saturation step returns minimal
        generators
      * *note PairLimit: reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPairLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value infinity, Bound the number of s-pairs considered in
        the saturation step
      * *note Strategy: reesIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, Choose a strategy for the saturation step
      * Trim => ..., default value true
      * *note Variable: symmetricKernel_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value "w", Choose name for variables in the created
        ring
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

Let $M$ be an $R = k[x_1,\ldots,x_n]/J$-module (for example an ideal), and let
$mm=ideal vars R = (x_1,\ldots,x_n)$, and suppose that $M$ is a homomorphic
image of the free module $F$. Let $T$ be the Rees algebra of $M$. The call
specialFiberIdeal(M) returns the ideal $J\subset{} Sym(F)$ such that $Sym(F)/J
\cong{} T/mm*T$; that is, $specialFiberIdeal(M) = reesIdeal(M)+mm*Sym(F).$

The name derives from the fact that $Proj(T/mm*T)$ is the special fiber of the
blowup of $Spec R$ along the subscheme defined by $I$.

With the default Trim => true, the computation begins by computing minimal
generators, which may result in a change of generators of M

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[a..h]                   |
|                                  |
|o1 = R                            |
|                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing               |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : M=matrix{{a,b,c,d},{e,f,g,h}}|
|                                  |
|o2 = | a b c d |                  |
|     | e f g h |                  |
|                                  |
|             2      4             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R              |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : analyticSpread minors(2,M)   |
|                                  |
|o3 = 5                            |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : specialFiberIdeal minors(2,M)|
|                                  |
|o4 = ideal(Z Z  - Z Z  + Z Z )    |
|            2 3    1 4    0 5     |
|                                  |
|o4 : Ideal of QQ[Z ..Z ]          |
|                  0   5           |
+----------------------------------+

If M is an n x n+1 matrix in n variables, and all generators have the same
degree d, with ell = n as expected, then the special fiber is a rational
hypersurface of degree $D := d^n$, and the reduction number is D-1.

+----------------------------------------+
|i5 : n = 2                              |
|                                        |
|o5 = 2                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i6 : x = symbol x                       |
|                                        |
|o6 = x                                  |
|                                        |
|o6 : Symbol                             |
+----------------------------------------+
|i7 : S = ZZ/32003[x_1..x_n]             |
|                                        |
|o7 = S                                  |
|                                        |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                     |
+----------------------------------------+
|i8 : M = matrix{{x_1,x_2,0},{0,x_1,x_2}}|
|                                        |
|o8 = | x_1 x_2 0   |                    |
|     | 0   x_1 x_2 |                    |
|                                        |
|             2      3                   |
|o8 : Matrix S  <-- S                    |
+----------------------------------------+
|i9 : I = minors(n,M)                    |
|                                        |
|             2         2                |
|o9 = ideal (x , x x , x )               |
|             1   1 2   2                |
|                                        |
|o9 : Ideal of S                         |
+----------------------------------------+
|i10 : specialFiber(I,I_0)               |
|                                        |
|        ZZ                              |
|      -----[w ..w ]                     |
|      32003  0   2                      |
|o10 = -------------                     |
|         2                              |
|        w  - w w                        |
|         1    0 2                       |
|                                        |
|o10 : QuotientRing                      |
+----------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Special fiber is here defined to be the fiber of the blowup over the subvariety
defined by the vars of the original ring. Note that if the original ring is a
tower ring, this might not be the fiber over the closed point! To get the
closed fiber, flatten the base ring first.



See also
========

  * *note reesIdeal: reesIdeal, -- Compute the defining ideal of the Rees
    Algebra

Ways to use specialFiberIdeal:
==============================

  * "specialFiberIdeal(Ideal)"
  * "specialFiberIdeal(Ideal,RingElement)"
  * "specialFiberIdeal(Module)"
  * "specialFiberIdeal(Module,RingElement)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note specialFiberIdeal: specialFiberIdeal, is a *note method
function with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

